  "fixes": [
    "Lifecycle admission and draining cover assisted and explicit manual merges before pause, structural index mutation, and shutdown; shutdown also drains producer bookkeeping.",
    "Known primary commit is tracked before derived completion. Retryable post-commit failures become CommitVisibilityNotSatisfied / ANTFLY_STALLED with a committed/do-not-retry diagnostic. Pre-commit batch refusal remains Busy. SDK guidance is updated without enum/schema changes.",
    "Ordinary coordinated read-only opens retain full allocator metadata frontiers. Logical data-only readers opt into that scope explicitly.",
    "Detached catalog/source pins close before physical maintenance. Bounded allocator service admits the current checkpoint through the fair writer queue; prepared vacuum keeps stale-tip rejection.",
    "Worthwhile shrink assessments retain a budgeted retry deadline across checkpoint refresh; canceled publication can retry without further growth. Scan retries wait at least 30 seconds or 64 times the prior scan duration."
  ],
